/home/worik/Documents/2026/hanihi/working/sessions/20260831-test-read-file/events.jsonl:9: {"kind":"turn_complete","ts":"2026-08-31T04:06:11.137761576Z","turn":1,"data":{"text":"Based on what I've explored, let me summarize the key constraints on what files I can read.\n\nThe tools available to me (`read_file`, `list_dir`, `grep`) operate on the **git repository**, and everything is filtered by the repo's ignore rules via the `ignore` crate. Let me lay out what this means concretely.\n\n## What I **can** read\n\nAny tracked (or untracked, non-ignored) file in the repo, including:\n\n- **Source code**: `crates/*/src/*.rs`, `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `crates/*/Cargo.toml`\n- **Docs/plans/specs**: `README.md`, `plans/*.md`, `prompts/*.md`, `evals/cases/*/README.md` and `case.toml`\n- **Session logs**: `working/sessions/*/events.jsonl`, `history.txt`, `session.json` (these live under `working/`, which is not ignored)\n- **Trace files**: `working/traces/**/*.cmd.json`\n- **Working notes/scratch**: `working/notes/*.md`, `working/applytest/*`, `working/scratch-repro/*`\n- And so on — basically the whole tree except what's ignored.\n\n## What I **cannot** read\n\nFiles matching the `.gitignore` / `.ignore` rules. From those two files:\n\n```gitignore\ntarget/\ntarget/doc/\n!target/doc/          # exception — target/doc IS readable\n*~\n.#*\n#*#\n```\n\n```ignore\ntarget/\n**/*.rs.bk\n```\n\nSo **git-ignored paths cannot be read, listed, or searched**. The main exclusion:\n\n- **`target/`** — the build output directory (with one exception: `target/doc/` is explicitly un-ignored via `!target/doc/`, so docs under it *are* accessible).\n- **`:ignore:` backup files** (`**/*.rs.bk`) — Rust source backups.\n- **Emacs temp files**: `*~`, `.#*`, `#*#`.\n\nNotably, **untracked-and-unignored files** *are* readable — ignore filtering (not `.git` status) is what governs access.\n\nBeyond ignore rules, there are also **policy limits** documented in the README: reads are capped at 64 KiB, and any path escaping the repo is refused. But those are size/scope constraints rather than \"can't read this file\" rules.\n\nIs there a specific file or area you'd like me to look at?","tool_calls":5}}
